Breadcrumb Home Academics Career outcomes and CORE Augustana grads are empowered to lead and live well in the world. Visit CORE at Augustana See student outcomes CORE (new) In This Section Directional Arrow Directional arrow Augie Choice sub-menu Directional Arrow Directional arrow Augie Choice General information For current students Career development sub-menu Directional Arrow Directional arrow Career development Overview Coaching and advising Career development portal Career outcomes Entrepreneurship Funding and scholarships Internships Student research Study abroad Success Teams More than just prepared for today's careers, they are problem-solvers with skillsets to match their dreams, able to make the new connections that the world needs most. Each year, Augustana's career development office surveys recent graduates to see how well they are beginning on their career paths. Most recently, 81% of the Class of 2025 responded with 95% positive career outcomes, including 66% employed, 22% in graduate school and 7% taking a purposeful gap year. How to start a dream job right after (or before) graduating from Augustana Three 2024 grads show what can happen with curiosity, internships, good challenges and support from their Augustana success team. Read the Story Directional Arrow Directional arrow 95% Employed or in graduate school within six months (2025) Directional Arrow Directional arrow 84% Graduates completed at least one internship (Class of 2025) Directional Arrow Directional arrow Augustana's CORE: Careers, Opportunities, Research, Exploration Because your greatest sources of joy and satisfaction are different from every other person’s, your career path should align with who you are. Augustana's CORE will help you make that happen. At CORE you’ll find a customized network of mentors and advisors, resources and learning experiences focused on your success—including career and life paths, graduate school, internships, study abroad, research, entrepreneurship and commitments to the community. Grow with Augustana Career development Use our unique Viking Score career-readiness program to chart your progress. Find the connections between academic choices and personal interests, skills and work values. Work with a career coach. Research and scholarship Research provides an original contribution to a field in a way that can be shared. • Conduct lab research with peers • Create a portfolio of art or music • Develop a market analysis Internships An internship is the practical application of the skills, knowledge and talents you gain at Augustana. Discover more about yourself in a work or volunteer setting. Unique programs EDGE student-entrepreneurs connect with community organizations in need of communications, marketing and creative services. The Upper Mississippi Center mobilizes students to help communities solve social, economic, and environmental challenges. Study abroad Whether it's a summer, a semester or our unique January term, Augie students study abroad for all the right reasons: for expanded academic learning and the appreciation of different places and cultures. Faculty-led programs combine the best of classroom learning and travel experience. Augie Choice Augie Choice guarantees students the opportunity for the kinds of learning that will make them stand out when they start careers or go on to graduate school. All students may apply for $2,000 to support a hands-on learning experience they choose: internship, research or study abroad. Contact CORE Visit CORE is located in the Olin Center in central campus. (map) Mailing address 639 38th St. Rock Island, Ill. 61201 Phone 309-794-7339 CORE staff directory Visit Apply Get info Augustana College 639 38th Street Rock Island, Ill., 61201 (map) 800-798-8100 309-794-7000 © 2026 Augustana College. All rights reserved. Social Media Facebook Facebook Icon Circle with Facebook's F Instagram Instagram Round icon with Instagram Logo TikTok TikTok Round Icon with TikTok logo LinkedIn LinkedIn Round Icon with LinkedIn logo Twitter Twitter X Round Icon with Twitter X logo Youtube YouTube Round icon with YouTube logo Quick Links Contact Academic calendar Blogustana Bookstore Complaint policy Disability & Access Resources Employment Graduate program Housing insecurity resources Library Magazine Maps and directions Non-discrimination Privacy Sitemap Title IX Locations and Facilities Building directory Augustana Convenient Care Augustana Center for Visual Culture Brunner Theatre Center Fryxell Geology Museum John Deere Planetarium Roseman Center for Speech, Language, and Hearing Swenson Swedish American Research Center Thomas Tredway Library Ticket Office Trinity College of Nursing & Health Sciences"
