    "https://www.augustana.edu/academics/core/careers": {
      "title": "Utility navigation",
      "description": "Career development tools for students | Augustana College Skip to main content Utility navigation Prospective Students Parents Alumni & Friends Faculty & Staff Current Students Trinity Students Augustana College Logo for Augustana College Home Open Menu Open Search About Open Directional Arrow Directional arrow News Rankings and recognition Offices and services Office of the President Events At a glance Campus map Virtual tour Quad Cities Blogustana Mission Employment opportunities Academics Open Directional Arrow Directional arrow Majors, minors and areas of study Study abroad Catalog Registrar Library Academic Resource Collective Disability & Access Resources Academic calendar Faculty-staff directory Academic centers Admissions Open Directional Arrow Directional arrow Request information Scholarships Financial aid Estimating net price and merit scholarships Our campus in photos Tuition deposit Apply Visit Transfer Graduate students Virtual visit Arts Open Directional Arrow Directional arrow Art Music Theatre Arts Center for Visual Culture Ticket Office Athletics Open Directional Arrow Directional arrow Athletics at Augustana Academic All-Americans Athletics homepage Campus Life Open Directional Arrow Directional arrow Residential Life Dining Counseling services Student support Campus Ministries Groups and activities Campus recreation Culture and connection International students Public Safety Dean of Students Career Paths Open Directional Arrow Directional arrow Student outcomes Augie Choice Internships Viking Score and career tools Signature programs Study abroad For employers Student research Give to Augustana Open Directional Arrow Directional arrow Make a gift Augustana Endowment Legacy planning Gift acceptance policy The Augustana Fund Friends of Music Your gifts at work Donor Bill of Rights The Gerber Grand Challenge in Philanthropy Viking Club Match your gift Meet the team Prospective Students Parents Alumni & Friends Faculty & Staff Current Students Trinity Students Breadcrumb Home Academics CORE CORE (new) In This Section Directional Arrow Directional arrow Augie Choice sub-menu Directional Arrow Directional arrow Augie Choice General information For current students Career development sub-menu Directional Arrow Directional arrow Career development Overview Coaching and advising Career development portal Career outcomes Entrepreneurship Funding and scholarships Internships Student research Study abroad Success Teams Career development tools for students Online and virtual career development resources Team members in Career Development & Vocation, part of CORE (Careers, Opportunities, Research, Exploration), are available to provide comprehensive career education and professional development resources, services, and programs for Augustana students and recent graduates. Career Development & Vocation partners with students by providing career coaching, curated resources and networks, and opportunities for career readiness skill development so that they may develop personalized pathways leading to lives of purpose and meaning. Explore and access curated tools and resources at careers.augustana.edu . Not sure where to start? Start Here: Your Career Journey Begins Quick links Resumes and cover letters Job search Internship search Interview prep Exploring careers and majors Graduate/professional school Post-grad service Online career tools Viking Score Track Your Progress. Earn Rewards. Launch Your Future. The Viking Score is Augustana’s career-readiness program designed to support you through college and into post-grad life. By completing key experiences and tracking your progress, you’ll earn points, and incentives, while building a strong foundation for your future. Whether you’re exploring options, preparing your tools, gaining experience, or launching your job or grad school search, the Viking Score helps you stay on track and recognize your achievements. How it works Complete activities in any of the four Viking Score stages Earn points throughout each academic year Activities include worksheets, coaching conversations, events, and more Submit your completed activities using the reporting form below Points are tallied through April 1 for graduating seniors seeking the graduation cord and banquet invitation and May 1 for all other students. Check your score and pick up your incentives before graduation! → Learn more about your Viking Score → Check your Viking Score → Report Viking Score Activities Handshake for jobs and internships Your all-in-one platform for job searches, internships, events, and career resources, available 24/7. Whether you’re exploring career paths, building your resume, or looking for your next big opportunity, Handshake is your go-to tool to make it happen. Accessing your account Students: Log in using your Augustana email and password — https://augustana.joinhandshake.com/ Faculty & Staff: You have access too! If you can’t sign in, contact us for help. Accounts are updated each semester to ensure access stays current Explore what you can do in Handshake Find jobs and internships Browse thousands of local, national, and remote opportunities tailored to your major, interests, and experience level. → Explore jobs and internships Register for career fairs and events See what’s happening on and off campus—from employer info sessions to career fairs and networking events. → View upcoming events Schedule an appointment Meet with a career coach to get help with resumes, interviews, grad school planning, or career exploration. → Schedule an appointment Need help using Handshake? Handshake FAQs Handshake support guides Handshake blog posts Internships An internship is the practical application of the skills, knowledge and talents that students gain at Augustana or discover about themselves in a work or volunteer setting. Internships at Augustana carry learning goals and objectives, plus an assessment at the conclusion of the internship. Internships may be part-time or full-time, paid or unpaid, for academic credit or non-credit. Learn more about specific types of internships Learn how to find an internship Search internship openings Registering internships at Augustana College Career fairs and career events Employers, recruiters, and graduate/professional programs and schools often gather at career fairs to provide an opportunity for job seekers to meet in one location. Employers may be recruiting for specific job openings or may wish to connect with participants to provide information on the company and future employment opportunities. Graduate/professional programs and schools want to share details about all they have to offer. View upcoming career fairs and events Prepare for virtual and in-person career fairs and events Extra tips for virtual fairs Career coaching Career coaching is a student-centered partnership between student and career coach designed to assist the student in developing career management skills while meeting the student’s career goals. Individual career coaching appointments are available to students and recent graduates regarding all areas of career planning and preparation. Appointments can be scheduled online through Handshake , our online career platform. Schedule an Appointment Who is my Career Coach? Appointment topics Visit Apply Get info Augustana College 639 38th Street Rock Island, Ill., 61201 (map) 800-798-8100 309-794-7000 © 2026 Augustana College. All rights reserved. Social Media Facebook Facebook Icon Circle with Facebook's F Instagram Instagram Round icon with Instagram Logo TikTok TikTok Round Icon with TikTok logo LinkedIn LinkedIn Round Icon with LinkedIn logo Twitter Twitter X Round Icon with Twitter X logo Youtube YouTube Round icon with YouTube logo Quick Links Contact Academic calendar Blogustana Bookstore Complaint policy Disability & Access Resources Employment Graduate program Housing insecurity resources Library Magazine Maps and directions Non-discrimination Privacy Sitemap Title IX Locations and Facilities Building directory Augustana Convenient Care Augustana Center for Visual Culture Brunner Theatre Center Fryxell Geology Museum John Deere Planetarium Roseman Center for Speech, Language, and Hearing Swenson Swedish American Research Center Thomas Tredway Library Ticket Office Trinity College of Nursing & Health Sciences"
